    "result_text": "All references are consistent with the new signature. The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'`, and every value derived from it follows the new identity.\n\n**Core changes:**\n- **`CustomerCodeGenerator`** \u2014 rewritten to build `<REGION>-<HASH8>`: REGION is the owner's canonical region; HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`. The per-city sequence number is gone.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 now passes the region (resolved from postcode/city) plus the already-E.164-normalized telephone and last name, instead of the old city/lastName/count.\n- **`Owner.getLocality()`** \u2014 now projects the REGION segment off the customer-code identity (falling back to region resolution only when no code is assigned yet), moving locality onto the new identity.\n\n**Ripple effects that needed no code change** \u2014 they already derive from `customerCode`, so they moved automatically: the membership number (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), its Luhn check digit, and the audit record (verified in the run: `AUDIT - Owner created ... customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\n**Structural hygiene (reuse, single responsibility):**\n- Extracted `Sha256.hex(...)` as one shared hashing helper, used by both `CustomerCodeGenerator` and `HouseholdIdGenerator` (removed the duplicated digest code from the latter).\n- Extracted `RegionResolver.regionFor(postcode, city)` as the single source of truth for region derivation (postcode-preferred, city fallback), used by both the generator path and `getLocality()` so the code's region and the derived locality can never disagree.\n\nThe target `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
